---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons errors -h <==
Which addon most likely throws Lua errors, how often, and whether an update may fix it (from
BugGrabber)

Usage: omaddons errors [OPTIONS]
       omaddons errors <COMMAND>

Commands:
  dismiss  Mark the errors read as seen, every client's or -t's: they stop being new (it cannot be
           undone)

Options:
      --since <WHEN>   Only errors seen since then: 30m, 12h, 1d, 2w, or an RFC 3339 time
      --addon <ADDON>  Only one addon's errors (by addon or folder name)
      --limit <N>      Addons shown per client [default: 10]
      --received       Also list the errors other players sent through BugSack, apart
      --raw-details    Also show messages, locals and code as written (they may hold names)
      --check          Exit 6 when a client has new errors, or could not be read completely

Examples:
  omaddons errors                       which addon throws Lua errors, on every client
  omaddons errors -t retail --since 1d  one client, the last day only
  omaddons errors dismiss -t retail     mark what was read as seen

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons errors --help <==
Which addon most likely throws Lua errors, how often, and whether an update may fix it (from
BugGrabber)

Usage: omaddons errors [OPTIONS]
       omaddons errors <COMMAND>

Commands:
  dismiss  Mark the errors read as seen, every client's or -t's: they stop being new (it cannot be
           undone)

Options:
      --since <WHEN>
          Only errors seen since then: 30m, 12h, 1d, 2w, or an RFC 3339 time

      --addon <ADDON>
          Only one addon's errors (by addon or folder name)

      --limit <N>
          Addons shown per client [default: 10]

      --received
          Also list the errors other players sent through BugSack, apart

      --raw-details
          Also show messages, locals and code as written (they may hold names)

      --check
          Exit 6 when a client has new errors, or could not be read completely

Examples:
  omaddons errors                                  every client, newest first
  omaddons errors --since 1d --json                the last day, for an agent
  omaddons errors -t retail --addon WeakAuras -v   one addon, every frame
  omaddons errors --check                          exit 6 on new errors

Messages an addon wrote itself may hold other players' names: they show only
with --raw-details. Errors other players sent through BugSack are counted apart.

See also: errors dismiss, update, status

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the
                         Classic Era client), family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every
                         client) [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change
                         nothing)
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by
                         commands that change nothing)
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
